X-WR-TIMEZONE:America/New_York
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Purple Rain
DTSTART:20270313T003000Z
DTEND:20270313T030000Z
DTSTAMP:20261018T075443Z
UID:1010794
DESCRIPTION:<p>Experience Prince&rsquo\;s legacy live on stage at Broadway
 &rsquo\;s Majestic Theatre in <em>Purple Rain</em>\, the electrifying new 
 musical based on the Grammy&reg\;-winning album and Oscar&reg\;-winning fi
 lm\, featuring over 20 of his iconic hits\, including &ldquo\;When Doves C
 ry\,&rdquo\; &ldquo\;I Would Die 4 U\,&rdquo\; &ldquo\;Take Me with U\,&rd
 quo\; and &ldquo\;The Beautiful Ones.&rdquo\;<br /><br />Minneapolis\, 198
 4. A new era of music television is creating overnight stars. A magnetic y
 oung performer known as &ldquo\;The Kid&rdquo\; seems like the perfect fro
 ntman to lead his bandmates to stardom. But when his past threatens everyt
 hing he&rsquo\;s built\, he&rsquo\;ll have to sing his way out of the dark
 ness and into the spotlight where he belongs.<br /><br />A visionary creat
 ive team reimagines Prince&rsquo\;s extraordinary world for the stage\, wi
 th direction by Tony&reg\;-nominated director Saheem Ali (<em>Buena Vista 
 Social Club</em>)\, acclaimed librettist and screenwriter Peter Duchan (Do
 gfight)\, Emmy&reg\;-winning choreographer Ebony Williams (<em>Sneakerella
 </em>\, additional choreography for the Renaissance World Tour)\, a music 
 team led by Tony Award winner Jason Michael Webb (<em>MJ the Musical</em>)
 \, and longtime Prince collaborators and bandmates Bobby Z and Morris Haye
 s?as Prince music advisors.</p>
LOCATION:Majestic Theatre\, 245 West 44th St\, New York NY 10036
END:VEVENT
